riscv: add a driver for the OpenComputers II mid-level API

OC2 computers expose their mid-level API ("oc2,mlapi") as a page of
byte-wide registers that programs drive directly, plus an interrupt that
is raised while events are queued. OC2's Linux image binds the generic
uio_pdrv_genirq driver to it.

Provide the same interface as /dev/mlapi: mmap(2) maps the register page,
read(2) of 4 bytes blocks until the interrupt fired and returns how many
times it has fired, write(2) of a 32-bit 1 re-enables the interrupt (it is
disabled each time it fires), and poll(2) reports when a read would not
block.

